  "title": "PhysMRV: Physical Memory Retrieval and Verification for Physics Plausibility Reasoning",
  "summary": "PhysMRV addresses the limitations of video-language models in physical plausibility reasoning by transforming training videos into a structured memory bank, enabling frozen VLMs to verify physical plausibility without additional training. It evaluates on benchmarks like ImplausiBench, IntPhys2, and GRASP Level 2, demonstrating its effectiveness across diverse VLMs.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "PhysMRV uses a hierarchical memory bank comprising scene descriptions, physical-event graphs, and physics-rule summaries to enhance physical plausibility reasoning.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "It evaluates on three challenging benchmarks and shows consistent improvements over direct prompting across state-of-the-art VLMs.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "PhysMRV transforms training videos into structured physical knowledge rather than relying on semantic similarity for context.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
